to fetch.\n\n**Outcome.** A0 finding E4 is confirmed and extended, a composition rule for both modes is derived from the tagged source, and one unexpressible constraint is recorded. No ax call, no ax PR or spec repository was touched, no code was written in the launcher. The report and probe are attached as three task outcome resources, and the task is in `to-review`.\n\n**What the tagged source says** (skill-agents-management v0.5.10, commit 13d167e):\n\n- Plan.Env is the plugin's complete child environment over `LaunchRequest.Env`, not a delta. The launcher SPEC and Decision 0013 both overlay \"inherited ⊕ plan Env\", which re-admits every name the plugin removed.\n- Beyond E4's wording, every plugin also removes the six `TASK_BOARD_*` run-context keys when the request carries no run context, which a terminal launch never does. Codex additionally rewrites PATH.\n- Over an empty parent, ChildEnv returns exactly the plugin's own names. At this tag with no run context that set is empty, so no plugin writes the home variable.\n- BuildPlan with an empty Env is refused by `ErrNoPath`, so the own-name set has to come from a direct ChildEnv call, not a second plan.\n\n**The rule I recommend.** Layer 1 is the plan request's input, never a composition layer. Untracked mode execs Plan.Env plus fragment env plus the variable channel. Tracked mode builds the plan over the real environment but fills `env_literals` only from ChildEnv over an empty parent, plus fragment env and channel. No inherited value, PATH, or secret can enter the document by construction, and no diffing is needed. The env_names collision rule stays as written but must subtract those own-name literals rather than Plan.Env, otherwise every inherited name would be dropped from env_names and the destination lookup silently disabled.\n\n**Contract limit.** The closed launch-plan document has no member for \"unset this name on the destination\", so the plugin strip list cannot reach a tracked child. If ax's terminal backend hands the child `CLAUDECODE=1`, the claude child refuses as nested. Whether ax's own plugins strip it was not read and is reported as unknown. This is a recorded residual, not a pending product decision; a future ax `env_unset` member would close it.\n\n**Evidence.** A five-test probe against the fetched v0.5.10 module passed 5/5 with exit 0, including a negative test showing the naive \"all Plan.Env into env_literals\" rule leaks a seeded inherited secret. Six deterministic tests for the implementation story are specified in the report, with the narrowing bound named at the composer call site.\n\n**Two things to flag for the reviewer.** The report is 8.3 KB against the 6 KB aim; the sources and test list did not compress further without losing anchors. Checklist items 3 through 9 are generic decomposition gates; I checked them because this task created no board elements, and the report's last section says the follow-up split, one spec erratum task and one composer task, is the story owner's call after review.","ttft_ms":2348,"type":"result","duration_ms":377389,"uuid":"44121170-529b-49a1-a194-349cbca8353a","ttft_stream_ms":1503,"time_to_request_ms":22,"first_content_frame_ms":1730,"queued_turn_count":0}
